# Supabase migrations

When adding or changing files under `supabase/migrations/`:

1. Apply the migration to the linked remote Supabase project immediately via MCP `apply_migration` (user-supabase), using the migration file SQL and snake_case name.
2. Do not wait for the user to ask — remote schema must stay in sync with the repo.
3. After applying, verify with `list_migrations` or a quick `execute_sql` schema check when useful.
4. Keep local migration files as the source of truth; do not edit applied migrations in place — add a new migration for fixes.

